  "result": "I found the cause and wrote up a fix, but haven't changed any code because plan mode is active.\n\n**Cause:** `join_options` in `src/click/formatting.py:319` sorts an option's names with `reverse=True`. Long names come out before short ones, so help shows `--help, -h` instead of `-h, --help`. The existing tests at `tests/test_commands.py:188-190` already expect the short-first form.\n\n**Planned fix:**\n- Change line 319 to `rv.sort(key=lambda x: x[0])`. The sort is stable, so names with the same prefix length keep their declaration order.\n- Add a regression test in `tests/test_formatting.py` checking that `join_options([\"--long\", \"-l\"])` returns `(\"-l, --long\", False)`.\n- Run `tests/test_formatting.py`, `tests/test_commands.py` and `tests/test_options.py`, then the full suite.\n\nThe plan is saved at `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\the-help-output-looks-toasty-hennessy.md`. I couldn't submit it for approval because the plan-approval tool isn't available here. If you meant a different ordering problem, such as the order of options between lines, tell me and I'll re-check.",
